#!/bin/sh
# release-stage: a release flow's three scripted stages. It is kept for a
# future stored release flow and is not run today: footplate's releases are
# cut by hand with scripts/release.sh (docs/building.md, "Building"). Such a
# flow would run it as the cmd of an exec group routed for build, verify and
# publish (one group with the stage in cmd: scripts/release-stage $YARDR_STAGE).
#
#   scripts/release-stage <build|verify|publish>
#
# It reads the bead from the environment the exec runner gives it (YARDR_BEAD,
# YARDR_DEPOT_PATH, YARDR_BASE, YARDR_BIN), like yardr's
# contrib/deploy/deploy-dokku, and the version from the bead's title's last
# word, which must be v<major>.<minor>.<patch>; the bead's body is the
# release notes.
#
#   build: refuses a bad title (question: the bead is wrong), a version that
#     is not Cargo.toml's, an existing release or tag, a dirty tree, and a
#     checkout that is not the remote's base; builds the archives and
#     checksums.txt into a private dir; tags the base commit, pushes the
#     tag, and makes the GitHub release with the bead's body as its notes;
#     notes the five signing commands for the version on the bead. Then
#     done, to sign. A run that died after tagging resumes: a tag at the
#     base commit with no release on it is finished, not refused.
#   verify: downloads the release, checks checksums.txt.minisig against the
#     release key and the archives against checksums.txt, then checks each
#     macOS archive: each zip is unpacked and its app must be notarized
#     (xcrun stapler validate, and spctl naming Notarized Developer ID as
#     the source), and each disk image must be stapled and notarized
#     itself, mount read-only holding the app and the Applications link,
#     and hold a notarized app. Then done, to publish, the note saying
#     what was checked, or that none was and why; a missing or bad
#     signature reports failed with what minisign said, so sign is asked
#     again, and archives that do not match, an app or image that is not
#     notarized, or a required check that could not run, report question,
#     to decide. A missing Mac tool skips just that check, and the done
#     note says so.
#   publish: files the yardr.dev sync bead and advances it to new, notes its
#     id on the release bead. Then done, to published.
#
# Every failure path ends in a done with an outcome or a hold, never a bare
# exit, as deploy-dokku documents: has_outcome asks prime before moving, so
# only moves the flow allows are tried, and a flow that names none holds
# the bead instead.
#
# Needs on PATH: jq and git always; gh for build and verify; minisign and
# shasum (or sha256sum) for verify, and xcrun, spctl, ditto and hdiutil,
# which a Mac has, for verify's look at the macOS archives (off a Mac the
# note says that look was skipped). gh acts as whoever it is logged in as.
# The build runs scripts/release.sh, so on a Mac, where that builds. That takes
# the Windows zip from the run of the Windows workflow for the base commit with
# the gh above, waiting for the run if it is going, unless
# FOOTPLATE_RELEASE_WINDOWS=off is in the environment this runs in, in which
# case the release ships without the Windows zip and the stage expects the
# six other archives. It also signs and notarizes the macOS apps and disk
# images when
# FOOTPLATE_RELEASE_SIGN_IDENTITY and FOOTPLATE_RELEASE_NOTARY_PROFILE are in
# the environment this runs in, which the exec group takes from its env_file
# (docs/building.md "Building"); the build's note says which it was. Needs
# this Mac logged in, with the keychain that holds the identity unlocked.
#
# Vendored from yardr's contrib/release/stage (yardr@a3870526) with
# footplate's release as the default: one checkout holds the whole release,
# and no release depends on what a sibling yardr clone has checked out. A
# fix upstream is mirrored here, and a fix here belongs upstream too. The
# release (repo, build, key) still comes from the environment, with
# footplate's as the defaults.
#
#   YARDR_RELEASE_REPO      the GitHub repo, owner/name (default yardr-dev/footplate)
#   YARDR_RELEASE_BUILD     the build command, run in the depot as
#                           $BUILD <version> <out-dir>, writing the archives
#                           and checksums.txt there (default scripts/release.sh)
#   YARDR_RELEASE_PUBKEY    the minisign public key verify checks against
#                           (default the release key, which signs yardr's
#                           releases and footplate's alike)
#   YARDR_RELEASE_KEY_PATH  the signer's secret key, as the five commands
#                           name it (default ~/.minisign/yardr-release.key,
#                           the one key that signs yardr's releases and
#                           footplate's alike)
#   YARDR_RELEASE_REMOTE    the git remote the tag is fetched from and pushed
#                           to (default origin)
set -u
# The ranges in the patterns below are ASCII's, and what git and gh say is
# read in English.
export LC_ALL=C
MODE=${1:-}
: "${YARDR_BEAD:?not run by an exec group}"
Y=${YARDR_BIN:-yardr}
BEAD=$YARDR_BEAD
REPO=${YARDR_DEPOT_PATH:-}
BASE=${YARDR_BASE:-}
GHREPO=${YARDR_RELEASE_REPO:-yardr-dev/footplate}
PRODUCT=${GHREPO##*/}
PUBKEY=${YARDR_RELEASE_PUBKEY:-RWSzUPGBbv7MDqH+nnbNmYdOm20UTkuk7eC5e6XuVtYRwZtaEZRlV/WB}
BUILD=${YARDR_RELEASE_BUILD:-scripts/release.sh}
# The default keeps its ~ on every shell: quoted, it expands for whoever
# pastes the commands, not here (bash would expand an unquoted one, dash
# would not, and the note must read the same everywhere).
KEYPATH=${YARDR_RELEASE_KEY_PATH:-"~/.minisign/yardr-release.key"}
REMOTE=${YARDR_RELEASE_REMOTE:-origin}

# has_outcome <name>: whether the flow offers outcome <name> from here, asked
# of prime before moving, as merge-local asks (no jq: only sh, git and yardr
# are promised for the asking), so that only moves the flow allows are tried.
has_outcome() {
  "$Y" prime --bead "$BEAD" --json |
    sed -n '/^  "next": {/,/^  }/p' |
    sed -n '/^    "outcomes": \[/,/^    \]/p' |
    grep -q "^        \"name\": \"$1\""
}
# Each outcome is one move with its note. Moving ends this session (the
# daemon stops the script), so it is always the last thing done.
# done_with <stage> <note>: the flow's done outcome, else the stage by name.
done_with() {
  echo "== $BEAD: $2"
  if has_outcome done; then
    printf '%s\n' "$2" | "$Y" bead done "$BEAD" --note - && exit 0
  fi
  printf '%s\n' "$2" | "$Y" bead advance "$BEAD" --to "$1" --note -
  exit 0
}
hold() {
  echo "== hold $BEAD: $1"
  "$Y" bead note "$BEAD" "$MODE: $1"
  "$Y" bead hold "$BEAD"
  exit 0
}
# fail <outcome> <one line> [<more>]: the flow's outcome with the whole
# note; a flow that names none holds the bead instead.
fail() {
  outcome=$1
  text=$2
  if [ $# -gt 2 ]; then
    text="$text
$3"
  fi
  echo "== $BEAD $outcome: $2"
  if has_outcome "$outcome"; then
    printf '%s\n' "$MODE: $text" | "$Y" bead done "$BEAD" --outcome "$outcome" --note - && exit 0
  fi
  hold "$text"
}

case "$MODE" in
build | verify | publish) ;;
*)
  hold "run as the cmd of an exec group with the stage in it (scripts/release-stage \$YARDR_STAGE), not as '$*'"
  ;;
esac
# A dir depot has no tags and no base to build; a route that hands one over
# is a mistake in the depot's flow, as it is for merge-local.
if [ "${YARDR_DEPOT_KIND:-git}" = dir ]; then
  hold "depot ${YARDR_DEPOT:-?} is a dir depot, with no tags to release; route its stages to other groups"
fi
if ! command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  fail failed "jq is not on PATH; the release group runs where jq, git and gh are"
fi

tmp=""
cleanup() {
  [ -z "$tmp" ] || rm -rf "$tmp"
}
trap cleanup EXIT
maketmp() {
  if ! tmp=$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/release-stage.XXXXXX"); then
    tmp=""
    if [ "$MODE" = verify ]; then
      fail question "cannot make a working directory; nothing was checked"
    fi
    fail failed "cannot make a working directory; nothing was released"
  fi
}

# version <outcome>: the bead's title's last word in $v (and the bead's
# show --json in $show), refused unless v<major>.<minor>.<patch>. A bad one
# is a question about the bead itself, for a person to fix; a bead that
# cannot be read reports <outcome>.
version() {
  show=$("$Y" bead show "$BEAD" --json) || fail "$1" "reading the bead failed; nothing was released"
  title=$(printf '%s' "$show" | jq -r '.title // empty')
  title=$(printf '%s' "$title" | sed 's/ *$//')
  v=${title##* }
  # grep matches line by line, so a title with a newline in its last word
  # is refused here first: only the version, whole, reaches a tag, gh or
  # the signing commands.
  case $v in *[!v0-9.]*) v_ok="" ;; *) v_ok=1 ;; esac
  [ -n "$v_ok" ] && printf '%s\n' "$v" | grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$' ||
    fail question "the bead's title names no version (its last word is \"$v\"): title it \"$PRODUCT v<major>.<minor>.<patch>\" and advance the bead back to $MODE"
}

build() {
  : "${YARDR_DEPOT_PATH:?the bead has no depot}" "${YARDR_BASE:?the bead has no base}"
  command -v git >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail failed "git is not on PATH; the release group runs where jq, git and gh are"
  command -v gh >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail failed "gh is not on PATH (and logged in); the release group runs where jq, git and gh are"
  version failed
  echo "== $BEAD: build $v of $GHREPO from $BASE"
  # The body is the release notes; an empty one would make a release that
  # says nothing.
  body=$(printf '%s' "$show" | jq -r '.body // empty')
  [ -n "$body" ] || fail question "the bead has no body, which is the release notes: write them on it and advance the bead back to build"
  [ -z "$(git -C "$REPO" status --porcelain)" ] ||
    fail failed "$REPO has uncommitted or untracked files; commit or clean them, then advance the bead back to build"
  # The version is Cargo.toml's, as scripts/release.sh requires: it would
  # refuse the build itself, but the run is refused here, before anything
  # is fetched or tagged, with what to do about it. Parsed as release.sh
  # parses it, so the two cannot disagree.
  number=${v#v}
  toml=$(sed -n 's/^version = "\(.*\)"$/\1/p' "$REPO/Cargo.toml" | head -n 1)
  [ "$number" = "$toml" ] ||
    fail failed "the bead titles $v, which is not Cargo.toml's version (v$toml) in $REPO: title the bead for v$toml, or land the version bump first, then advance the bead back to build"
  fetch_out=$(git -C "$REPO" fetch -q "$REMOTE" "$BASE" 2>&1) ||
    fail failed "fetching $REMOTE/$BASE in $REPO failed: $fetch_out. Nothing was tagged."
  base=$(git -C "$REPO" rev-parse --verify -q "refs/remotes/$REMOTE/$BASE^{commit}") ||
    fail failed "$REMOTE/$BASE is not a branch $REPO knows after fetching; nothing was tagged"
  head=$(git -C "$REPO" rev-parse --verify -q 'HEAD^{commit}') ||
    fail failed "reading HEAD in $REPO failed; nothing was tagged"
  [ "$head" = "$base" ] ||
    fail failed "$REPO is at $(git -C "$REPO" rev-parse --short "$head"), not at $REMOTE/$BASE ($(git -C "$REPO" rev-parse --short "$base")): check out $BASE there and pull, then advance the bead back to build"
  at=$(git -C "$REPO" rev-parse --short "$base")
  # A run that died after tagging resumes: the tag is ours when it is at
  # this base and no release stands on it, and tagging and pushing it again
  # change nothing. Anything else already standing is refused.
  if gh release view "$v" --repo "$GHREPO" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    fail failed "release $v already exists on $GHREPO: if a run left it half-made, upload what is missing by hand and advance the bead to sign"
  fi
  tagat=$(git -C "$REPO" rev-parse --verify -q "refs/tags/$v^{commit}" 2>/dev/null || true)
  if [ -n "$tagat" ] && [ "$tagat" != "$base" ]; then
    fail failed "tag $v already exists in $REPO, at another commit ($(git -C "$REPO" rev-parse --short "$tagat")): delete it or title the bead for another version"
  fi
  maketmp
  out=$tmp/dist
  cache=$tmp/gocache
  mkdir "$out" "$cache"
  log=$tmp/build.log
  echo "== $BEAD: $BUILD $v (out $out)"
  # The build runs in the depot, so a relative build command is the depot's
  # own script; the out-dir is private to the run, so what is released is
  # what this run built. GOCACHE is private too, for builds that use Go.
  if (cd "$REPO" && GOCACHE="$cache" "$BUILD" "$v" "$out" >"$log" 2>&1); then
    echo "== $BEAD: built $v"
  else
    fail failed "building $v failed" "$(tail -n 30 "$log")"
  fi
  [ -f "$out/checksums.txt" ] || fail failed "the build left no checksums.txt in $out; nothing was tagged"
  # This depot's release has seven fixed archive names, six with
  # FOOTPLATE_RELEASE_WINDOWS=off, which releases without the Windows zip.
  # Do not publish a partial build or let an unexpected file ride along as
  # a release asset.
  if [ "${FOOTPLATE_RELEASE_WINDOWS:-}" = off ]; then
    windows_wanted=""
    n=6
    count="six"
  else
    windows_wanted=1
    n=7
    count="seven"
  fi
  files=""
  for f in \
      "Footplate_${number}_darwin_arm64.zip" \
      "Footplate_${number}_darwin_amd64.zip" \
      "Footplate_${number}_darwin_arm64.dmg" \
      "Footplate_${number}_darwin_amd64.dmg" \
      "footplate_${number}_linux_arm64.tar.gz" \
      "footplate_${number}_linux_amd64.tar.gz" \
      "footplate_${number}_windows_amd64.zip"; do
    if [ -z "$windows_wanted" ] && [ "$f" = "footplate_${number}_windows_amd64.zip" ]; then
      continue
    fi
    [ -f "$out/$f" ] || fail failed "the build left no $f in $out; nothing was tagged"
    files="$files
$f"
  done
  for f in "$out"/*; do
    [ -f "$f" ] || continue
    b=${f##*/}
    case $b in
    checksums.txt | \
    "Footplate_${number}_darwin_arm64.zip" | \
    "Footplate_${number}_darwin_amd64.zip" | \
    "Footplate_${number}_darwin_arm64.dmg" | \
    "Footplate_${number}_darwin_amd64.dmg" | \
    "footplate_${number}_linux_arm64.tar.gz" | \
    "footplate_${number}_linux_amd64.tar.gz") ;;
    "footplate_${number}_windows_amd64.zip")
      [ -n "$windows_wanted" ] ||
        fail failed "the build left unexpected file $b in $out; expected six archives and checksums.txt"
      ;;
    *) fail failed "the build left unexpected file $b in $out; expected $count archives and checksums.txt" ;;
    esac
  done
  [ -z "$tagat" ] || echo "== $BEAD: tag $v is already at $at; finishing that run"
  [ -n "$tagat" ] || git -C "$REPO" tag "$v" "$base" || fail failed "tagging $at as $v failed; nothing was pushed"
  git -C "$REPO" push "$REMOTE" "$v" >"$tmp/push.log" 2>&1 ||
    fail failed "tag $v is made but pushing it to $REMOTE failed; push it by hand, then advance the bead back to build" "$(tail -n 10 "$tmp/push.log")"
  printf '%s\n' "$body" >"$tmp/notes.md"
  # The asset list is the fixed filenames, so pass it from inside the
  # output directory; a TMPDIR containing spaces stays one path.
  # shellcheck disable=SC2086 # $files is a newline-separated list
  if (cd "$out" && gh release create "$v" $files checksums.txt --repo "$GHREPO" --title "$v" --notes-file "$tmp/notes.md" --verify-tag >"$tmp/create.log" 2>&1); then
    echo "== $BEAD: released $v"
  else
    fail failed "tag $v is pushed but making the release failed; make it by hand from $out, or delete the tag and the release and advance the bead back to build" "$(cat "$tmp/create.log")"
  fi
  url="https://github.com/$GHREPO/releases/tag/$v"
  dir="~/releases/$v"
  # What the build made of the macOS apps and disk images, from what it was
  # given: scripts/release.sh signs, notarizes and staples them when both
  # signing variables are set, and signs the apps ad hoc and leaves the
  # images unsigned when neither is (half a pair failed the build above). The
  # variables come from the group's environment, so a group that lacks them
  # would release apps another Mac blocks, without a word; the note says it
  # before the checksums are signed.
  if [ -n "${FOOTPLATE_RELEASE_SIGN_IDENTITY:-}" ] && [ -n "${FOOTPLATE_RELEASE_NOTARY_PROFILE:-}" ]; then
    mac="The macOS apps and disk images are signed with Developer ID, notarized by Apple and stapled."
  else
    mac="The macOS apps are signed ad hoc and not notarized, and the disk images are not signed (FOOTPLATE_RELEASE_SIGN_IDENTITY and FOOTPLATE_RELEASE_NOTARY_PROFILE are not set where this group runs), so another Mac blocks them."
  fi
  done_with sign "build: $PRODUCT $v is released ($url, built from $at): $n archives and checksums.txt, the checksums not yet signed. $mac Sign the checksums with the five commands, in order (minisign asks for the key's password; each names $v):

mkdir -p $dir
gh release download $v --repo $GHREPO --pattern checksums.txt --dir $dir --clobber
minisign -S -s $KEYPATH -m $dir/checksums.txt
minisign -V -P $PUBKEY -m $dir/checksums.txt
gh release upload $v --repo $GHREPO $dir/checksums.txt.minisig --clobber

Then Done: the verify stage checks the signature next."
}

# dmg_detach: let go of the disk image macs() has mounted, if one is;
# the EXIT trap's half, so a check that fails with an image attached
# still detaches it. An attached image outlives the script.
dmg_detach() {
  if [ -n "${dmg_mounted:-}" ]; then
    hdiutil detach "$dmg_mounted" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
    dmg_mounted=""
  fi
}

# macs: the macOS archives of the downloaded release, looked at as a Mac
# that takes them would. Each *_darwin_*.dmg must have its ticket stapled
# (xcrun stapler validate) and be taken by Gatekeeper as notarized (spctl
# -a -vv -t open names the source), then mounts read-only at a mount
# point of its own, since both images are named Footplate, and must hold
# exactly Footplate.app and the Applications link to /Applications (a
# .DS_Store may ride along); the mounted app passes stapler and spctl
# -a -vv -t exec in turn. Each *_darwin_*.zip is unpacked with ditto,
# into a directory of its own since every zip holds a Footplate.app, and
# the app must have its ticket stapled and be taken by Gatekeeper as
# notarized. A fault is a question, as an archive that does not match
# is: the release is remade by hand. A release built without the signing
# variables is signed ad hoc and fails here, which is meant. Sets $mac
# to the sentence the done note carries: what was checked, or why none
# was, so that a skipped check is never silent. xcrun, spctl, ditto and
# hdiutil are a Mac's; where one the release needs is missing, the check
# is skipped. The download carries no quarantine, so mounting its images
# opens nothing flagged; no check clears any.
macs() {
  have_zips=""
  have_dmgs=""
  for f in "$tmp"/*_darwin_*.zip; do
    [ -f "$f" ] && have_zips=1 && break
  done
  for f in "$tmp"/*_darwin_*.dmg; do
    [ -f "$f" ] && have_dmgs=1 && break
  done
  if [ -z "$have_zips$have_dmgs" ]; then
    mac="The release holds no macOS archive, so no app was checked for notarization."
    return
  fi
  missing=""
  for tool in xcrun spctl; do
    command -v "$tool" >/dev/null 2>&1 || missing="${missing:+$missing, }$tool"
  done
  if [ -n "$have_zips" ]; then
    command -v ditto >/dev/null 2>&1 || missing="${missing:+$missing, }ditto"
  fi
  if [ -n "$have_dmgs" ]; then
    command -v hdiutil >/dev/null 2>&1 || missing="${missing:+$missing, }hdiutil"
  fi
  if [ -n "$missing" ]; then
    if [ -n "$have_zips" ] && [ -n "$have_dmgs" ]; then
      what="The macOS apps and disk images were not checked for notarization"
    elif [ -n "$have_dmgs" ]; then
      what="The macOS disk images were not checked for notarization"
    else
      what="The macOS apps were not checked for notarization"
    fi
    mac="$what: PATH here lacks $missing, which a Mac has, so that check was skipped."
    return
  fi
  remade="it is remade by hand (the release and the tag deleted, the bead back to build)"
  # The images first, so a release whose images fail is questioned on
  # them; each mount is let go of on the way out, whatever happened in
  # between, and each image's own detach clears the mount the trap
  # would let go of.
  dmg_mounted=""
  trap 'dmg_detach; cleanup' EXIT
  dchecked=""
  for dmg in "$tmp"/*_darwin_*.dmg; do
    [ -f "$dmg" ] || continue
    b=${dmg##*/}
    out=$(xcrun stapler validate "$dmg" 2>&1) ||
      fail question "the disk image $b of release $v does not pass xcrun stapler validate (a release built without the signing variables leaves its images unsigned, with no ticket stapled); $remade" "$out"
    out=$(spctl -a -vv -t open --context context:primary-signature "$dmg" 2>&1) ||
      fail question "Gatekeeper refuses the disk image $b of release $v (spctl -a -vv -t open failed); $remade" "$out"
    case $out in
    *"source=Notarized Developer ID"*) ;;
    *) fail question "Gatekeeper does not take the disk image $b of release $v as notarized (spctl does not name source=Notarized Developer ID); $remade" "$out" ;;
    esac
    mount=$tmp/mount-${b%.dmg}
    mkdir "$mount" || fail question "cannot make a working directory; the macOS disk images were not checked"
    hdiutil attach -readonly -nobrowse -noautoopen -mountpoint "$mount" "$dmg" >"$tmp/mac.log" 2>&1 ||
      fail question "mounting $b of release $v failed; the macOS disk images were not checked" "$(cat "$tmp/mac.log")"
    dmg_mounted=$mount
    [ -d "$mount/Footplate.app" ] ||
      fail question "the disk image $b of release $v holds no Footplate.app; $remade"
    link=$(readlink "$mount/Applications" 2>/dev/null) || link=""
    [ "$link" = "/Applications" ] ||
      fail question "the disk image $b of release $v holds no Applications link to /Applications; $remade"
    extra=""
    for entry in "$mount"/* "$mount"/.[!.]* "$mount"/..?*; do
      [ -e "$entry" ] || [ -L "$entry" ] || continue
      e=${entry##*/}
      case $e in
      Footplate.app | Applications | .DS_Store) ;;
      *) extra="${extra:+$extra, }$e" ;;
      esac
    done
    [ -z "$extra" ] ||
      fail question "the disk image $b of release $v holds more than the app and the Applications link ($extra); $remade"
    out=$(xcrun stapler validate "$mount/Footplate.app" 2>&1) ||
      fail question "the Footplate.app in $b of release $v does not pass xcrun stapler validate; $remade" "$out"
    out=$(spctl -a -vv -t exec "$mount/Footplate.app" 2>&1) ||
      fail question "Gatekeeper refuses the Footplate.app in $b of release $v (spctl -a -vv -t exec failed); $remade" "$out"
    case $out in
    *"source=Notarized Developer ID"*) ;;
    *) fail question "Gatekeeper does not take the Footplate.app in $b of release $v as notarized (spctl does not name source=Notarized Developer ID); $remade" "$out" ;;
    esac
    hdiutil detach "$mount" >/dev/null 2>&1 ||
      fail question "letting go of $b of release $v after checking it failed"
    dmg_mounted=""
    dchecked="${dchecked:+$dchecked, }$b"
  done
  checked=""
  for zip in "$tmp"/*_darwin_*.zip; do
    [ -f "$zip" ] || continue
    b=${zip##*/}
    dest=$tmp/mac-${b%.zip}
    mkdir "$dest" || fail question "cannot make a working directory; the macOS apps were not checked"
    ditto -x -k "$zip" "$dest" >"$tmp/mac.log" 2>&1 ||
      fail question "unpacking $b of release $v failed; the macOS apps were not checked" "$(cat "$tmp/mac.log")"
    found=""
    for app in "$dest"/*.app; do
      [ -d "$app" ] || continue
      found=1
      name=${app##*/}
      out=$(xcrun stapler validate "$app" 2>&1) ||
        fail question "the $name in $b of release $v does not pass xcrun stapler validate (a release built without the signing variables is signed ad hoc, with no ticket stapled); $remade" "$out"
      out=$(spctl -a -vv -t exec "$app" 2>&1) ||
        fail question "Gatekeeper refuses the $name in $b of release $v (spctl -a -vv -t exec failed); $remade" "$out"
      case $out in
      *"source=Notarized Developer ID"*) ;;
      *) fail question "Gatekeeper does not take the $name in $b of release $v as notarized (spctl does not name source=Notarized Developer ID); $remade" "$out" ;;
      esac
      checked="${checked:+$checked, }$name in $b"
    done
    [ -n "$found" ] || fail question "$b of release $v holds no .app to check; $remade"
  done
  if [ -n "$checked" ] && [ -n "$dchecked" ]; then
    mac="The macOS apps and disk images are notarized (xcrun stapler validate passes and spctl names Notarized Developer ID as the source): $checked; $dchecked."
  elif [ -n "$dchecked" ]; then
    mac="The macOS disk images are notarized (xcrun stapler validate passes and spctl names Notarized Developer ID as the source): $dchecked."
  else
    mac="The macOS apps are notarized (xcrun stapler validate passes and spctl names Notarized Developer ID as the source): $checked."
  fi
}

verify() {
  command -v gh >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail question "gh is not on PATH (and logged in); the release group runs where jq, gh and minisign are"
  command -v minisign >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail question "minisign is not on PATH; the release group runs where jq, gh and minisign are"
  if command -v shasum >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    sum="shasum -a 256"
  elif command -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    sum="sha256sum"
  else
    fail question "neither shasum nor sha256sum is on PATH; the release group runs where one of them is"
  fi
  version question
  echo "== $BEAD: verify $v of $GHREPO"
  maketmp
  gh release download "$v" --repo "$GHREPO" --dir "$tmp" >"$tmp/download.log" 2>&1 ||
    fail question "downloading release $v failed; nothing was checked" "$(cat "$tmp/download.log")"
  [ -f "$tmp/checksums.txt" ] || fail question "release $v holds no checksums.txt; it is remade by hand (the release and the tag deleted, the bead back to build)"
  [ -f "$tmp/checksums.txt.minisig" ] ||
    fail failed "checksums.txt.minisig is not on release $v yet: run the five commands in the build's note, then Done again"
  # The signature covers the checksums, and the checksums cover each
  # archive; both are checked, in that order.
  minisign_out=$(minisign -V -P "$PUBKEY" -m "$tmp/checksums.txt" 2>&1) ||
    fail failed "the signature on release $v is bad" "$minisign_out"
  # shellcheck disable=SC2086 # $sum is a list
  (cd "$tmp" && $sum -c checksums.txt >check.log 2>&1) ||
    fail question "the archives of release $v do not match its checksums.txt; it is remade by hand (the release and the tag deleted, the bead back to build)" "$(cat "$tmp/check.log")"
  names=$(sed -n 's/^[0-9a-fA-F][0-9a-fA-F]*  *[* ]\{0,1\}\(.*\)$/\1/p' "$tmp/checksums.txt")
  n=$(printf '%s\n' "$names" | grep -c .) || n=0
  [ "$n" -gt 0 ] || fail question "release $v's checksums.txt names no files; it is remade by hand (the release and the tag deleted, the bead back to build)"
  # And nothing rides along that the checksums do not cover.
  extra=""
  for f in "$tmp"/*; do
    [ -f "$f" ] || continue
    b=${f##*/}
    case $b in
    checksums.txt | checksums.txt.minisig | download.log | check.log) continue ;;
    esac
    printf '%s\n' "$names" | grep -q -x -F "$b" || extra="$extra $b"
  done
  [ -z "$extra" ] ||
    fail question "release $v holds files its checksums.txt does not name ($extra); it is remade by hand (the release and the tag deleted, the bead back to build)"
  macs
  done_with publish "verify: the signature on $v is good ($minisign_out) and its $n archives match checksums.txt. $mac"
}

publish() {
  : "${YARDR_DEPOT_PATH:?the bead has no depot}"
  command -v git >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail failed "git is not on PATH; the release group runs where jq and git are"
  version failed
  echo "== $BEAD: publish $v of $GHREPO"
  maketmp
  at=$(git -C "$REPO" rev-parse --short --verify -q "refs/tags/$v^{commit}" 2>/dev/null) ||
    fail failed "tag $v is not in $REPO; fetch it, then advance the bead back to publish"
  url="https://github.com/$GHREPO/releases/tag/$v"
  day=$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
  if [ "$PRODUCT" = yardr ]; then other=footplate; else other=yardr; fi
  # Where the sync leaves the site's latest.json: yardr's at the root, every
  # other product's under its own name, as scripts/sync-release writes them.
  if [ "$PRODUCT" = yardr ]; then
    latest="public/releases/latest.json"
    site="https://yardr.dev/releases/latest.json"
  else
    latest="public/releases/$PRODUCT/latest.json"
    site="https://yardr.dev/releases/$PRODUCT/latest.json"
  fi
  title="Sync $PRODUCT $v to yardr.dev: scripts/sync-release $PRODUCT $v"
  body="$PRODUCT $v is released ($url, built from $at) and its checksums.txt.minisig is uploaded and verified against the release key on $day.

Run, from the depot's checkout: \`scripts/sync-release $PRODUCT $v\` (fetches the release with gh from $GHREPO, verifies the signature and the archives, replaces the previous $PRODUCT release directory with $v/ and rewrites $latest). Commit what it wrote. Nothing else changes.

Done when: the depot's test command passes; \`git diff main --stat\` shows only public/releases/ (the $PRODUCT paths, not $other's). After the deploy, $site names $v and the page offers it."
  new=$(printf '%s' "$body" | "$Y" bead create "$title" -d yardr.dev -p 1 -b - -l difficulty:1,size:small --json 2>"$tmp/create.err" | jq -r '.id // empty') || new=""
  [ -n "$new" ] || fail failed "filing the sync bead failed" "$(cat "$tmp/create.err")"
  "$Y" bead advance "$new" --to new || fail failed "sync bead $new is filed but advancing it to new failed; advance it by hand, then this bead to published"
  "$Y" bead note "$BEAD" "publish: filed $new (\"$title\") and advanced it to new."
  done_with published "publish: $new carries the site's sync; $PRODUCT $v is published."
}

case "$MODE" in
build) build ;;
verify) verify ;;
publish) publish ;;
esac
